So in this problem I had to find max consecutive one's.
To do that I just looped over the array and inc the count after every one and using max(result,count) to get the highest count .
And if nums[i] != 1  make count = 0

code---
class Solution {
public:
    int findMaxConsecutiveOnes(vector<int>& nums) {
        int count =0;
        int result = 0;
        for(int i = 0;i<nums.size();i++){
            if(nums[i]==1){
                count++;
            }
            result = max(count,result);
            if(nums[i]!=1){
                count = 0;
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
};
Time complexity = O(n)
max fn takes O(1) time complexity.
